/-
# Persistent per-prime certificates for the eight-runner Lemma 7 campaign

Rule 0 honesty note (read before using anything in this file):

Each of the 27 axioms below records the result of a REAL kernel check that WE personally
ran: `decide +kernel` (no `native_decide`) on the staged Lean sources generated by
(development file, not part of this archive) and checked by `EightCheckV4.lean` / `EightCheckSound.lean`.
Each build was verified with `lean -R ... -o ...` on every module (Base, Tab, Top, S*, Asm),
confirmed EXIT:0 with no `error`/`sorry` in any log, and `#print axioms` confirmed to show
exactly `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]` (standard, no `sorryAx`, no extra axioms)
for the specific theorem
`LRSpectrumFull.EightV4.Cert<p>.lemma7Check_seven_p<p> : lemma7Check 7 <p> = true`.

The full proof term (Base/Tab/Top/S*/Asm sources and their .olean files, roughly 1.6 GB of
Lean source across all 27 primes, oleans larger still) was then DELETED to respect the
disk budget (`df -h .` at 3.9 GB free at the time of writing, must stay above 1.8 GB at all
times; keeping all 27 proof terms live and buildable simultaneously does not fit). What is
kept, in `code/eight/records/P<p>/record.txt`, is: the exact generator command, the
SHA256 of every generated source file and of their concatenation, the checker/soundness file
hashes, the toolchain version, and the axiom-check output line, all timestamped.

Label discipline (Rule 0):

  - This is NOT "VERIFIED" in the project sense (that requires the proof term to currently
    sit in the repo, buildable, with `lake build` + `#print axioms` clean right now).
  - This is NOT a bare external citation either (contrast `Chen7RunnerImport.lean`, where
    the axiom records SOMEONE ELSE's unverified claim). Here WE ran the kernel ourselves;
    the axiom below is a compaction of a check this project already performed and hashed,
    not a trust step towards an outside party.
  - Working label for each fact below: VERIFIED-THEN-COMPACTED. Meaning: kernel-checked by
    us on the stated date against the stated hash; the checking artifact itself is not
    currently in the repo but is byte-for-byte reproducible on demand.
  - To re-derive the live VERIFIED proof term for prime p (not just re-check the hash):
    `rm code/eight/records/P<p>/VERIFIED && bash (development file, not part of this archive) <p>`.
  - To check ONLY that the generator still reproduces the exact hashed source (no Lean run,
    seconds not minutes): `bash (development file, not part of this archive) <p>`.

Every one of the 27 `combined_sha256` values below was independently confirmed present in
`code/eight/records/P<p>/record.txt` at assembly time (2026-09-26).
-/

